{"step_index":127,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:42:11Z","thinking":"**Considering the k=1 case**\n\nProving the base case `k=0` is straightforward; now the focus shifts to `k=1`.  Need to determine the equivalent statement for `k=1`. Aiming to find the necessary lemma to prove the `largestDegreeSum` property for this value. The general form of the statement requires careful consideration of the input parameter `k`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\\nlemma largestDegreeSum_one_lt {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hV : 2 ≤ Fintype.card V) :\\n    GraphCalc.largestDegreeSum G 1 < Fintype.card V := by\\n  unfold GraphCalc.largestDegreeSum\\n  cases h : ((Finset.univ.powersetCard 1).image (fun s => ∑ v ∈ s, G.degree v)).max with\\n  | top =>\\n    -- here getD gives 0\\n    have : 0 < Fintype.card V := by omega\\n    exact this\\n  | coe m =>\\n    -- here getD gives m\\n    have hm : m ∈ ((Finset.univ.powersetCard 1).image (fun s => ∑ v ∈ s, G.degree v)) := by\\n      exact?\\n    sorry\\n\"","Description":"\"Test exact? on max_mem\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_8ca1b27c/scratch.lean\"","toolAction":"\"Write file\"","toolSummary":"\"Test max_mem in scratch.lean\""}}]}
