{"step_index":139,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:44:03Z","thinking":"**Assembling Pieces for Proof**\n\nThe previous lemma, `largestDegreeSum_one_lt`, has been successfully proven. The focus shifts to assembling the pieces within `scratch.lean` to prove `Candidate`. The plan is to trace the proof, beginning with `minUpTo_ge`.\n\n\n**Tracing Proof Application**\n\nThe proof starts by unfolding definitions of `GraphCalc.minUpTo`, then uses a case split on the minimum of a filtered range. The lemmas `largestDegreeSum_zero` and `largestDegreeSum_one_lt` provide important building blocks. Finally, `minUpTo_ge` is applied within the `prove_8ca1b27c` theorem to prove `Candidate`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nset_option maxRecDepth 10000\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\\nabbrev Candidate : Prop :=\\n    ∀ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj],\\n      GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G → GraphCalc.HasSubTotalDominationNumber G → 2 ≤ GraphCalc.subTotalDominationNumber G\\n\\nlemma minUpTo_ge {n : ℕ} {p : ℕ → Prop} [DecidablePred p] (h_empty : 2 ≤ n)\\n    (h_elem : ∀ k ∈ (Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p, 2 ≤ k) :\\n    2 ≤ GraphCalc.minUpTo n p := by\\n  unfold GraphCalc.minUpTo\\n  cases h : ((Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p).min with\\n  | top =>\\n    exact h_empty\\n  | coe k =>\\n    exact h_elem k (Finset.mem_of_min h)\\n\\nlemma largestDegreeSum_zero {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\\n    GraphCalc.largestDegreeSum G 0 = 0 := by\\n  unfold GraphCalc.largestDegreeSum\\n  simp\\n  rfl\\n\\nlemma largestDegreeSum_one_lt {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (hV : 2 ≤ Fintype.card V) :\\n    GraphCalc.largestDegreeSum G 1 < Fintype.card V := by\\n  unfold GraphCalc.largestDegreeSum\\n  cases h : ((Finset.univ.powersetCard 1).image (fun s => ∑ v ∈ s, G.degree v)).max with\\n  | bot =>\\n    have : 0 < Fintype.card V := by omega\\n    exact this\\n  | coe m =>\\n    have hm : m ∈ ((Finset.univ.powersetCard 1).image (fun s => ∑ v ∈ s, G.degree v)) :=\\n      Finset.mem_of_max h\\n    rcases Finset.mem_image.mp hm with ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩\\n    rcases Finset.mem_powersetCard.mp hs with ⟨-, hs_card⟩\\n    rcases Finset.card_eq_one.mp hs_card with ⟨v, rfl⟩\\n    simp only [Finset.sum_singleton]\\n    exact G.degree_lt_card_verts v\\n\\ntheorem prove_8ca1b27c : Candidate := by\\n  intro V _ _ G _ hNontrivial _hHas\\n  unfold GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass at hNontrivial\\n  unfold GraphCalc.order at hNontrivial\\n  unfold GraphCalc.subTotalDominationNumber\\n  apply minUpTo_ge hNontrivial\\n  intro k hk\\n  rw [Finset.mem_filter] at hk\\\n<truncated 263 bytes>","Description":"\"Assemble full proof in scratch.lean\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_8ca1b27c/scratch.lean\"","toolAction":"\"Write file\"","toolSummary":"\"Test full proof in scratch.lean\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
